<title>HUNGARY: CESI index ends lower after three successive highs.</title>
<headline>CESI index ends lower after three successive highs.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index eased on Tuesday to close at 1,506.93 points, down 3.34 points or 0.22 percent, the Budapest Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The index closed lower after reaching three successive highs as most shares in the index basket closed lower or remained steady.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects trends of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410</p>
